Subject: [PATCH] docs: add Wasmer Edge deploy option

---
 README.md | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1f3b392..8f41d13 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -89,6 +89,12 @@ Assuming [Jekyll] and [Bundler] are installed on your computer:
 
 Just upload all the files in the directory `_site`.
 
+To build and host the site on [Wasmer Edge](https://docs.wasmer.io/edge/) instead:
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=just-the-docs%2Fjust-the-docs-template)
+
+The button imports this public template repository; it does not create a copy in your GitHub account. To customize your site and redeploy on push, first create your own repository from this template, then import that repository in Wasmer. Set `url` in `_config.yml` to your site's address.
+
 ## Customization
 
 You're free to customize sites that you create with this template, however you like!
